<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρύπτω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>El.</u>
			150
		</span></i>: fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρύψω </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατα-</span>)
			v.l.in
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			5.42
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Rufin.
		</span></i>): aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔδρυψα,</span>
		
			Ep.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρύψα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.324
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				243
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατα-,</span> tm.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				655
			</span></i> (lyr.): aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρυψάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.153
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.2
			</span></i> (Antip. Sid.): plpf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέδρυπτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					14.391
				</span></i>
			:—<i>tear, strip,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βραχίονα δουρὸς ἀκωκὴ δρύψ᾽ ἀπὸ
					μυώνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
				</span></i>
			 l. c.:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρυψαμένω δ᾽ ὀνύχεσσι παρειὰς
				ἀμφί τε δειράς</span>
			<i>tearing each other's</i> cheeks and necks all round, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i> l. c.: mostly in sign of mourning, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρύπτεν κάρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					150
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκάτερθε παρειάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.672
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρύπτεσθαι παρειάν</span>
			<i>to tear one's</i> cheek, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				655
			</span></i>; without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρειάν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				3.1.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν δὲ χοῖρον αὐονὴ δρύπτει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					8.2
				</span></i>
			.—Poet., <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i> and later Prose, as <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				3.38
			</span></i>.</div>
